      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To complete the task, I need to create the specified Python files in the current working directory. Each scored implementation file must use a concrete external provider and make that provider identifiable in code. The local helper files may contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities. Here's the plan:\n\n1. Create `register_user.py` to register a new user using AWS Cognito.\n2. Create `email_password_login.py` to log in a user with email and password using AWS Cognito.\n3. Create `refresh_session.py` to refresh an expired session using AWS Cognito.\n4. Create `password_reset.py` to start a password reset flow using AWS Cognito.\n5. Create `identity_client.py` to provide local configuration and client helper utilities for Email/Password Account Lifecycle.\n6. Create `identity_models.py` to define local request, response, and normalization helpers for Email/Password Account Lifecycle.\n7. Create `welcome_translate.py` to translate onboarding copy into the user's locale using AWS Translate.\n8. Create `profile_moderation.py` to moderate profile text before account activation using AWS Comprehend.\n9. Create `onboarding_summary.py` to summarize onboarding state for support using AWS Textract.\n10. Create `profile_note_store.py` to persist onboarding notes and support metadata in a managed document store using AWS DynamoDB. </thinking>\n\n",
