        "text": "I have successfully created all the requested Python files in the current working directory. Here are the files I created:\n\n1. `register_user.py` - Creates a new email/password user account using AWS Cognito.\n2. `email_password_login.py` - Signs in a user with email and password and returns tokens using AWS Cognito.\n3. `refresh_session.py` - Refreshes an expired session or access token using AWS Cognito.\n4. `password_reset.py` - Starts a password reset flow for a local account using AWS Cognito.\n5. `identity_client.py` - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Email/Password Account Lifecycle.\n6. `identity_models.py` - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Email/Password Account Lifecycle.\n7. `welcome_translate.py` - Translates onboarding copy into the user's locale using AWS Translate.\n8. `profile_moderation.py` - Moderates profile text before account activation using AWS Comprehend.\n9. `onboarding_summary.py` - Summarizes onboarding state for support using AWS Textract.\n10. `profile_note_store.py` - Persists onboarding notes and support metadata in a managed document store using AWS DynamoDB.\n\nEach scored implementation file uses a concrete external provider and makes that provider identifiable in code. The local helper files contain configuration loading, payload normalization, or response parsing utilities when useful.",
